add("sleeptrain-1wr0c28", None, "partner", "toddler_12_24_months", "success_story", ["ferber", "partner_disagreement", "sleep_training_values"], "She adamantly refused sleep training but I had finally decided we were at our limit. Last night was night 4 of Ferber (I'm doing it solo) and LO slept through the night for 10.5 hours straight!", "Father of a 20-month-old after months of two-hour split nights; post title says mom refused for 9 months.")
add("sleeptrain-1wr0c28", "pc8km3m", "partner", "toddler_12_24_months", "belief", ["night_wakings"], "Kid has slept SO bad for so long that it didn't even cross my mind that it may be too much sleep now.", "Replying about the toddler's nap length after Ferber worked.")
add("sleeptrain-1wru3az", None, "parent_unspecified", "baby_5_8_months", "success_story", ["cry_it_out", "sleep_training_values"], "I never wanted to do CIO but we tried everything and one night after so many failed transfers and feeling exhausted, we finally gave in and tried it. My 8 month old has gone from sleeping on average 9.5-10 hours over 24 hours to now sleeping 10+ hours just overnight.", "Day 11 of cry-it-out.")
add("sleeptrain-1wru3az", None, "parent_unspecified", "baby_5_8_months", "pain", ["cry_it_out", "guilt"], "Will she ever go to sleep without crying? I still find it upsetting and just hoping one day she doesn’t get so upset at bedtime.", "Bedtime crying still 11-37 minutes after the method worked overnight.")
add("sleeptrain-1wrx8a1", None, "partner", "regression_4_months", "pain", ["bedtime_battle", "transition_to_cot"], "Before sleep training, bedtime was a complete battle. We would bounce/rock him on a yoga ball for a long time, as it was the only way he knew how to fall asleep, and even after he was asleep, we often needed multiple transfer attempts.", "Father's success write-up; baby held for every sleep until 3 months.")
add("sleeptrain-1wrx8a1", None, "partner", "regression_4_months", "success_story", ["ferber", "consistency_failure"], "nights 4 and 5 brought the extinction burst, with up to 50 minutes of crying on night 5. We were honestly about to give up at that point.", "Ferber started at 4 months after a week adjusting the schedule.")
add("sleeptrain-1wrx8a1", None, "partner", "regression_4_months", "success_story", ["ferber"], "as soon as we left him in the crib, he rolled onto his side, started sucking his thumb, and fell asleep in 3 minutes without any crying. We just couldn't believe it.", "Week 3 of Ferber.")
add("sleeptrain-1wrx8a1", None, "partner", "regression_4_months", "success_story", ["ferber", "partner_split_nights"], "being able to sit down and have dinner with my wife at night, watch a TV show together, and know that our little one is peacefully sleeping in his crib is something we didn't think would be happening anytime soon.", "The 'selfish' benefit the father names.")
add("sleeptrain-1wrx8a1", None, "partner", "regression_4_months", "advice_given", ["free_advice", "ferber"], "thanks to everyone on this sub who answered our questions along the way — reading other people's experiences definitely helped us stick with it when the first few nights were rough.", "What kept them going: other parents online.")
add("sleeptrain-1wrx8a1", "pdzjpre", "partner", "regression_4_months", "success_story", ["ferber", "short_naps"], "So in our experience, night sleep improved massively but naps didn't automatically follow. We're treating falling asleep independently and connecting nap cycles as two separate skills for now.", "Two weeks on, naps still 35-45 minutes.")
add("sleeptrain-1ws58sy", None, "new_mother", "baby_5_8_months", "success_story", ["ferber", "room_sharing", "regression_4_month"], "We still wanted to room sharing due to some logistical reasons. So we did Ferber with room sharing.", "5.5-month-old woke every half hour from 5am after the 4-month regression.")
add("sleeptrain-1ws58sy", None, "new_mother", "baby_5_8_months", "pain", ["ferber", "guilt"], "My husband and I both cried while hearing my son crying.", "Night one of Ferber, 15 minutes and two check-ins.")
add("sleeptrain-1ws58sy", None, "new_mother", "baby_5_8_months", "success_story", ["ferber", "room_sharing"], "Just wanted to share in case anyone here wants to do sleep training while room sharing - it’s possible!", "By night three under 10 minutes of crying.")
add("beyondthebump-1wsb5ix", None, "parent_unspecified", "baby_9_12_months", "pain", ["night_wakings"], "I do not want to sit up nursing and swinging her for an hour every night like she's a newborn. What happened to her ability to self soothe? To be soothed BY me?", "Trained at 5 months; at 9 months a new nightly 2-3am wide-awake screaming.")
add("sleeptrain-1wu1aof", None, "parent_unspecified", "baby_5_8_months", "pain", ["guilt", "sleep_training_values"], "But I feel so guilty. Every cry - even just a bleat - is like a gut punch.", "A month of training going 'objectively' well with a 6-month-old.")
add("sleeptrain-1wu1aof", None, "parent_unspecified", "baby_5_8_months", "belief", ["guilt", "sleep_training_values", "comparison_other_babies"], "Maybe it’s the stigma around sleep training? Most of my mum friends aren’t doing it.", "Why the guilt persists.")
add("sleeptrain-1wu1aof", None, "parent_unspecified", "baby_5_8_months", "success_story", ["sleep_training_values"], "I’m definitely a better parent now I’m sleeping at night and she’s happier in the day too.", "Despite the guilt.")
add("beyondthebump-1wu2fqt", None, "parent_unspecified", "baby_5_8_months", "belief", ["guilt", "cry_it_out"], "I think I thought there’s be zero crying by now.", "Cross-post of the guilt post, with one added line.")
add("beyondthebump-1wu2fqt", "pczfom6", "parent_unspecified", "baby_5_8_months", "pain", ["guilt", "sleep_training_values"], "Sleep training deleted my post. I think maybe I’ll delete this too.", "Her post on the sleep training subreddit was removed.")
add("sleeptrain-1wvx58k", None, "parent_unspecified", "regression_4_months", "success_story", ["cry_it_out", "wake_windows", "pacifier"], "Very happy with limited crying and believe its 100% due to the fact that schedule was overhauled before attempting.", "4.5-month-old; schedule fixed on commenters' advice, then cry-it-out and pacifier stopped.")
add("sleeptrain-1wvx58k", None, "parent_unspecified", "regression_4_months", "success_story", ["cry_it_out", "free_advice"], "We fixed the schedule like you all recommended, went to 2/2/2/2/2", "What turned it: free subreddit schedule advice.")
add("sleeptrain-1ww8p3j", None, "parent_unspecified", "baby_9_12_months", "success_story", ["cry_it_out", "feeding_to_sleep"], "He cried for 30 minutes the first night and we were just in disbelief, only 30 minutes!!?? THEN HE SLEPT THROUGH THE WHOLE NIGHT!!??", "11-month-old who needed movement and a bottle; bottle moved 30 minutes before bed.")
add("sleeptrain-1ww8p3j", None, "parent_unspecified", "baby_9_12_months", "success_story", ["cry_it_out", "maternal_exhaustion"], "I’ve had so much time to myself and actually feel rested after 11 months of broken sleep. Do yourself a favor and jump the gun.", "Three nights in.")
add("sleeptrain-1ww8p3j", None, "parent_unspecified", "baby_9_12_months", "fear", ["cry_it_out", "sleep_training_values"], "I was worried it would be a disaster considering he can never calm down if he gets himself worked up so cry it out always scared me.", "Doubts before starting.")
add("sleeptrain-1ww8p3j", "pdj9avr", "parent_unspecified", "baby_9_12_months", "regret", ["cry_it_out"], "that first full night we were seriously regretting not doing this a long long time ago 😂", "Reply to another parent.")
add("sleeptrain-1ww8p3j", "pdj8zkb", "parent_unspecified", "baby_9_12_months", "advice_given", ["feeding_to_sleep"], "I was breastfeeding my son to sleep for a really long time but honestly just replaced it with bottles so I could stop being his pacifier 😅", "Advice to a breastfeeding parent.")
add("NewParents-1wwfqr6", None, "new_mother", "baby_2_4_months", "success_story", ["maternal_exhaustion"], "It’s not always a perfect night or day. But it got better.", "Mother of a 3-month-old back at work, writing to give others hope.")
add("NewParents-1wxygrd", None, "parent_unspecified", "unknown", "success_story", ["app_tracking", "white_noise"], "I put on a story about the semicolon. He was out in 5-10 minutes. Even my husband falls asleep to it.", "Tried an adult sleep-stories app on vacation after another parent mentioned it.")
add("sleeptrain-1x12k4k", None, "experienced_mother", "regression_4_months", "success_story", ["book_purchase", "gentle_method"], "We’ve been following a gentle FIO approach, loosely based on Precious Little Sleep.", "Second daughter at 4.5 months now falls asleep independently; first child was trained at 7 months with modified CIO.")
add("sleeptrain-1x12k4k", None, "experienced_mother", "regression_4_months", "pain", ["night_wakings", "feeding_to_sleep"], "I feel like we’ve made such a massive step forward with independent sleep, but we’re not seeing the same improvement overnight yet.", "Still waking frequently; only breastfeeding settles her.")
add("sleeptrain-1x12k4k", None, "experienced_mother", "regression_4_months", "desire", ["night_wakings"], "I’d be delighted with two or three genuine feeds overnight and being able to settle her back into her cot between them!", "Realistic goal for a 20-week-old.")
add("sleeptrain-1x1amzb", None, "experienced_mother", "baby_2_4_months", "success_story", ["contact_naps", "transition_to_cot", "pacifier"], "After wearing or holding baby for every single nap up to 12 weeks I decided to try naps in the bassinet for one full day to see how it would go.", "Mother also caring for a 3-year-old; two days of bassinet naps.")
add("sleeptrain-1x1amzb", None, "experienced_mother", "baby_2_4_months", "pain", ["contact_naps"], "Having a 3 year old and being nap trapped all day was wearing me down.", "Why she tried.")
add("NewParents-1x2pein", None, "new_mother", "baby_5_8_months", "failure_story", ["consistency_failure", "cosleeping", "feeding_to_sleep"], "He was sleep trained at around 4.5 months and it went well for a few weeks before I started to “backslide” into co-sleeping, nursing to sleep, etc.", "First-time mother of a 6-month-old, travelling abroad.")
add("NewParents-1x2pein", None, "new_mother", "baby_5_8_months", "pain", ["guilt", "consistency_failure"], "I haven’t been good about following his usual bedtime routine while on vacation (we’re staying in a studio apartment) and it brings me great shame.", "Scared sleep will be ruined on return.")
add("sleeptrain-1x2t2vp", None, "parent_unspecified", "baby_5_8_months", "success_story", ["cry_it_out"], "First night he cried 10min then put himself to sleep. Since then no tears and he falls asleep in 10-15 min. Very grateful he was so receptive!", "Night CIO at 5 months, three weeks on.")
add("sleeptrain-1x2t2vp", None, "parent_unspecified", "baby_5_8_months", "pain", ["short_naps", "contact_naps", "conflicting_advice"], "We are ready to start on naps. My arms are crying from bouncing him to sleep.", "Naps still fed or bounced to sleep; parent cites 'so much conflicting advice'.")
